Offline Concurrent Versioned Morse Stream Decoder
Context
You are implementing an offline Morse decoder. The decoder receives chunks of boolean signal samples from any thread. true means tone is on. false means silence.
Chunks are analyzed on background worker threads. Chunks may arrive out of order, worker results may finish out of order, chunks may be replaced or removed by revision, and decoded output must always reflect the highest active revision of each chunk in sample-time order.
The hard part is concurrency correctness: worker jobs can become stale, replacement/removal can invalidate already decoded output, Morse runs can cross chunk boundaries, output events must be emitted exactly once, and the decoder must not solve every update by recomputing from sample 0.
Task
Implement ConcurrentMorseDecoder.

