Requirements
Use plain Kotlin/JVM and JDK concurrency primitives only. Do not use Android APIs, coroutines, RxJava, network APIs, microphone APIs, audio APIs, or third-party libraries.
The constructor must throw IllegalArgumentException if maxPendingJobs <= 0. Public methods may be called from any thread and must be thread-safe.
appendOrReplaceChunk requires chunkId to be non-empty, revision >= 0, and startSampleIndex >= 0; otherwise throw IllegalArgumentException.
Empty sample arrays are no-ops after argument validation. Non-empty sample arrays must be copied before appendOrReplaceChunk returns.
Each chunk covers the half-open range [startSampleIndex, startSampleIndex + samples.size). Range overflow must throw IllegalArgumentException.
Chunks may arrive out of order. Active chunks with different chunkIds must not overlap. An overlapping append must throw IllegalArgumentException without changing decoder state. Adjacent chunks are allowed.
For the same chunkId, a higher revision replaces the old active revision. Equal or lower revisions are ignored after argument validation. Replacing a chunk may change its range and sample data.
removeChunk(chunkId, revision) requires non-empty chunkId and revision >= 0. A remove with revision higher than the currently known revision removes the active chunk, if present. Equal or lower revisions are ignored.
Replacing or removing a chunk invalidates decoded output from the earliest affected sample onward. Already decoded output before that point must remain stable.
Each accepted non-empty append schedules background analysis for that chunk, subject to maxPendingJobs. At most maxPendingJobs worker jobs may be running at once. Extra accepted chunks must remain queued and be scheduled later in deterministic sample-order, then chunkId order.
Analysis converts the copied samples into tone/silence runs. Raw samples for a chunk must be discarded after that chunk successfully commits; pending or running chunks may retain their copied samples.
Worker results may finish out of order. A later chunk may commit before an earlier chunk, but decoded output may use only the longest contiguous committed prefix starting at sample index 0.
Tone or silence runs crossing adjacent chunk boundaries must be merged before Morse classification.
The decoder must maintain checkpoints and must not recompute decoded output from sample 0 after every commit, replacement, or removal. Re-decode may restart only from the nearest retained checkpoint at or before the earliest affected sample. debugState().decodeRestartSamples must record every restart sample used for re-decode.
setTiming(samplesPerDit, tolerancePercent) requires samplesPerDit > 0 and tolerancePercent in 0..49; otherwise throw IllegalArgumentException.
Calling setTiming increments the generation and clears active chunks, known revisions, queued jobs, running jobs, committed chunks, checkpoints, decoded output, and pending output events. Old worker results from previous generations must be ignored.
Calling clear() has the same reset behavior as setTiming, except it keeps the current timing values.
Morse timing uses samplesPerDit as one unit. Tone lengths within tolerance of 1 unit decode as .. Tone lengths within tolerance of 3 units decode as -. Other tone lengths make the current Morse character invalid.
The inclusive accepted tone range for n units is:
lower = ceil(n * samplesPerDit * (100 - tolerancePercent) / 100)
upper = floor(n * samplesPerDit * (100 + tolerancePercent) / 100)
Silence gaps use lower-bound separators. A silence run shorter than the accepted lower bound for 3 units is an intra-character gap. A silence run greater than or equal to the accepted lower bound for 3 units but shorter than the accepted lower bound for 7 units is a letter gap. A silence run greater than or equal to the accepted lower bound for 7 units is a word gap.
A trailing run at the end of the current contiguous committed prefix is provisional and must not be classified yet. This prevents prematurely decoding a tone or gap that may continue in a future adjacent chunk.
A character is emitted only when a finalized letter gap or word gap is observed. A word gap finalizes the current character, if any, and emits at most one space. Do not emit leading or duplicate spaces.
Unknown Morse patterns decode as '?'. A character containing any invalid tone run also decodes as '?'.
decodedText() returns a stable snapshot immediately. It must not wait for workers, schedule work, mutate state, or consume output events.
pollEvents() returns pending output events exactly once and clears the event queue. Calling pollEvents() repeatedly without new decoded-output changes must return an empty list.
If newly decoded text only extends the previous decoded text, emit MorseEvent.Append(sequence, text), where sequence is the previous text length. If a replacement, removal, or late commit changes already emitted text, emit MorseEvent.ReplaceFrom(sequence, text), where sequence is the first changed character offset and text is the new suffix from that offset.
debugState() returns a stable snapshot immediately. It must not wait for workers, schedule work, mutate state, consume events, or expose mutable internal collections.
The implementation must not deadlock under concurrent appendOrReplaceChunk, removeChunk, setTiming, clear, decodedText, pollEvents, debugState, and out-of-order worker completions.
Tests
Invalid inputs
Verify invalid maxPendingJobs, empty chunkId, negative revision, negative startSampleIndex, overflowing chunk range, invalid samplesPerDit, and invalid tolerancePercent throw IllegalArgumentException.
Input array copied and raw samples discarded
Append a chunk, mutate the source BooleanArray, complete the worker, and verify decoding uses the copied values. After commit, verify debugState().retainedSampleCount no longer includes that committed chunk’s raw samples.
Overlap rejected atomically
Append chunk A covering [0, 10). Attempt chunk B covering [5, 15) and verify it throws without changing active chunks. Verify chunk C covering [10, 20) is accepted.
Higher revision replaces old chunk
Append chunk A revision 1, commit it, then append chunk A revision 2 with different data. Verify revision 2 replaces revision 1, invalidates decoded output from the affected sample, and stale revision 1 worker results cannot commit afterward.
Equal or lower revision ignored
Append chunk A revision 2. Then append revision 1 and revision 2 again with different samples. Verify neither schedules new work nor changes decoded output.
Remove invalidates suffix
Decode text across several chunks, then remove a middle chunk with a higher revision. Verify decoded text rolls back to the longest valid prefix and a ReplaceFrom event is emitted.
Simple SOS decode
With samplesPerDit = 2, append chunks encoding ... --- ..., include valid letter gaps, and include a following opposite-valued run so the final gap is no longer trailing. Verify decodedText() is "SOS".
Out-of-order append and prefix gating
Append later chunks before earlier chunks. Complete later workers first. Verify decodedText() remains based only on the contiguous prefix from sample 0 and expands only when missing earlier chunks commit.
Out-of-order worker completion
Append chunks [0, n), [n, 2n), and [2n, 3n). Complete workers in order third, first, second. Verify final decoded text is timeline ordered.
Tone run crosses chunk boundary
Split one dah tone across adjacent chunks. Verify the merged tone decodes as -, not as separate dits or an invalid tone.
Silence run crosses chunk boundary
Split a letter gap across adjacent chunks. Verify the character is not emitted until the merged gap is finalized by a following opposite-valued run.
Word gap crosses chunk boundary
Split a 7-unit word gap across adjacent chunks. Verify exactly one space is emitted after the word gap is finalized.
Trailing run is provisional
Append a valid dit tone followed by silence, but make the silence run trailing at the end of the contiguous prefix. Verify no character is emitted until a later opposite-valued run arrives.
Unknown and invalid characters
Append an unmapped valid pattern such as ...... followed by a finalized letter gap and verify "?". Append a tone outside dit/dah tolerance followed by a finalized letter gap and verify "?".
Tolerance boundaries
With samplesPerDit = 10 and tolerancePercent = 30, verify tone lengths at accepted lower/upper boundaries decode correctly and just-outside lengths become invalid.
Gap threshold boundaries
Verify gaps just below the 3-unit lower bound are intra-character, gaps at the 3-unit lower bound are letter gaps, and gaps at the 7-unit lower bound are word gaps.
Backpressure
Set maxPendingJobs = 2, append many chunks, and verify only two jobs are submitted initially. Complete one job and verify exactly one queued chunk is scheduled next in deterministic order.
Clear rejects stale workers
Append chunks, keep workers blocked, call clear(), then complete old workers. Verify decoded text stays empty, committed chunks stay empty, and old output events do not appear.
Timing change rejects stale workers
Append chunks under one timing config, call setTiming, then complete old workers. Verify old results do not commit and decoded text remains empty.
New data after clear starts fresh
Append and clear. Then append new chunks starting at sample 0, complete them, and verify decoding works from a fresh generation.
Gap in committed chunks stops decoding
Commit chunks [0, 10) and [20, 30) while [10, 20) is missing. Verify decoded output and contiguousCommittedUntil stop at 10.
Exactly-once append events
Decode new characters, call pollEvents(), and verify an Append event. Call pollEvents() again without new commits and verify it returns empty.
Correction event after replacement
Decode text, poll events, replace an earlier chunk with data that changes the decoded suffix, complete the new worker, and verify pollEvents() returns one ReplaceFrom event rather than replaying all prior text.
No full recompute from sample 0
Commit many chunks and record decodeRestartSamples. Replace a chunk near the end. Verify the next re-decode restart sample is near the affected chunk checkpoint, not 0.
Snapshot safety
Call decodedText(), pollEvents(), and debugState() while workers are pending and blocked. Verify they return immediately and do not mutate unrelated state.
Concurrent stress
Randomly interleave appends, replacements, removals, clears, timing changes, worker completions, decodedText, pollEvents, and debugState. Verify no deadlocks, no stale commits, no duplicate events, no overlapping accepted ranges, and no output inconsistent with the highest active revisions.


Reference Solution

import java.util.TreeMap
import java.util.concurrent.Executor
import java.util.concurrent.Executors
import kotlin.math.ceil
import kotlin.math.floor
import kotlin.math.max

class ConcurrentMorseDecoder(
    private val analysisExecutor: Executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(2),
    private val maxPendingJobs: Int = 64
) {
    private val lock = Any()

    private var generation: Long = 0L
    private var samplesPerDit: Int = 10
    private var tolerancePercent: Int = 30

    private val knownRevisions = HashMap<String, Long>()
    private val records = HashMap<String, ChunkRecord>()
    private val rangesByStart = TreeMap<Long, String>()
    private val runningJobs = LinkedHashSet<JobKey>()

    private val checkpoints = TreeMap<Long, ParserState>()
    private val events = ArrayList<MorseEvent>()
    private val decodeRestartSamples = ArrayList<Long>()

    private var decoded: String = ""
    private var contiguousCommittedUntil: Long = 0L
    private var submittedJobCount: Long = 0L

    init {
        require(maxPendingJobs > 0) {
            "maxPendingJobs must be > 0"
        }
        checkpoints[0L] = ParserState()
    }

    fun appendOrReplaceChunk(
        chunkId: String,
        startSampleIndex: Long,
        samples: BooleanArray,
        revision: Long
    ) {
        validateChunkId(chunkId)
        require(revision >= 0) { "revision must be >= 0" }
        require(startSampleIndex >= 0) { "startSampleIndex must be >= 0" }

        if (samples.isEmpty()) return

        val size = samples.size.toLong()

        require(startSampleIndex <= Long.MAX_VALUE - size) {
            "chunk range overflows Long"
        }

        val endSampleIndex = startSampleIndex + size
        val copied = samples.copyOf()

        val jobs = synchronized(lock) {
            val known = knownRevisions[chunkId]
            if (known != null && revision <= known) {
                return
            }

            if (overlapsAnotherChunkLocked(startSampleIndex, endSampleIndex, chunkId)) {
                throw IllegalArgumentException("chunk overlaps active range")
            }

            val old = records[chunkId]
            val affectedStart = minOf(old?.start ?: startSampleIndex, startSampleIndex)

            if (old != null) {
                removeRecordLocked(old)
            }

            knownRevisions[chunkId] = revision

            val record = ChunkRecord(
                id = chunkId,
                start = startSampleIndex,
                end = endSampleIndex,
                revision = revision,
                status = ChunkStatus.Queued,
                samples = copied,
                analysis = null
            )

            records[chunkId] = record
            rangesByStart[startSampleIndex] = chunkId

            redecodeFromLocked(affectedStart)
            drainSchedulingLocked()
        }

        submitJobs(jobs)
    }

    fun removeChunk(chunkId: String, revision: Long) {
        validateChunkId(chunkId)
        require(revision >= 0) { "revision must be >= 0" }

        val jobs = synchronized(lock) {
            val known = knownRevisions[chunkId]
            if (known != null && revision <= known) {
                return
            }

            knownRevisions[chunkId] = revision

            val old = records[chunkId]
            if (old != null) {
                removeRecordLocked(old)
                redecodeFromLocked(old.start)
            }

            drainSchedulingLocked()
        }

        submitJobs(jobs)
    }

    fun setTiming(samplesPerDit: Int, tolerancePercent: Int) {
        require(samplesPerDit > 0) {
            "samplesPerDit must be > 0"
        }
        require(tolerancePercent in 0..49) {
            "tolerancePercent must be in 0..49"
        }

        synchronized(lock) {
            this.samplesPerDit = samplesPerDit
            this.tolerancePercent = tolerancePercent
            resetAllLocked()
        }
    }

    fun clear() {
        synchronized(lock) {
            resetAllLocked()
        }
    }

    fun decodedText(): String {
        return synchronized(lock) {
            decoded
        }
    }

    fun pollEvents(): List<MorseEvent> {
        return synchronized(lock) {
            val snapshot = events.toList()
            events.clear()
            snapshot
        }
    }

    fun debugState(): MorseDebugState {
        return synchronized(lock) {
            MorseDebugState(
                generation = generation,
                samplesPerDit = samplesPerDit,
                tolerancePercent = tolerancePercent,
                activeChunks = records.keys.toSet(),
                queuedChunks = records.values
                    .filter { it.status == ChunkStatus.Queued }
                    .map { it.id }
                    .toSet(),
                runningChunks = records.values
                    .filter { it.status == ChunkStatus.Running }
                    .map { it.id }
                    .toSet(),
                committedChunks = records.values
                    .filter { it.status == ChunkStatus.Committed }
                    .map { it.id }
                    .toSet(),
                decodedText = decoded,
                contiguousCommittedUntil = contiguousCommittedUntil,
                submittedJobCount = submittedJobCount,
                retainedSampleCount = records.values
                    .sumOf { it.samples?.size?.toLong() ?: 0L },
                decodeRestartSamples = decodeRestartSamples.toList()
            )
        }
    }

    private fun resetAllLocked() {
        generation++
        knownRevisions.clear()
        records.clear()
        rangesByStart.clear()
        runningJobs.clear()
        checkpoints.clear()
        checkpoints[0L] = ParserState()
        events.clear()
        decoded = ""
        contiguousCommittedUntil = 0L
        decodeRestartSamples.clear()
    }

    private fun validateChunkId(chunkId: String) {
        require(chunkId.isNotEmpty()) {
            "chunkId must be non-empty"
        }
    }

    private fun removeRecordLocked(record: ChunkRecord) {
        records.remove(record.id)
        rangesByStart.remove(record.start)
        runningJobs.remove(JobKey(record.id, record.revision))
    }

    private fun overlapsAnotherChunkLocked(
        start: Long,
        end: Long,
        sameChunkId: String
    ): Boolean {
        val previous = rangesByStart.floorEntry(start)
        if (previous != null && previous.value != sameChunkId) {
            val previousRecord = records[previous.value]
            if (previousRecord != null && previousRecord.end > start) {
                return true
            }
        }

        val next = rangesByStart.ceilingEntry(start)
        if (next != null && next.value != sameChunkId && next.key < end) {
            return true
        }

        return false
    }

    private fun drainSchedulingLocked(): List<AnalysisJob> {
        val jobs = ArrayList<AnalysisJob>()

        while (runningJobs.size < maxPendingJobs) {
            val next = records.values
                .asSequence()
                .filter { it.status == ChunkStatus.Queued }
                .sortedWith(compareBy<ChunkRecord> { it.start }.thenBy { it.id })
                .firstOrNull()
                ?: break

            val samples = next.samples ?: break

            val updated = next.copy(status = ChunkStatus.Running)
            records[next.id] = updated

            val key = JobKey(next.id, next.revision)
            runningJobs.add(key)

            submittedJobCount++

            jobs.add(
                AnalysisJob(
                    generation = generation,
                    id = next.id,
                    start = next.start,
                    end = next.end,
                    revision = next.revision,
                    samples = samples.copyOf()
                )
            )
        }

        return jobs
    }

    private fun submitJobs(jobs: List<AnalysisJob>) {
        for (job in jobs) {
            analysisExecutor.execute {
                val analysis = analyzeChunk(job)
                commitAnalysis(job, analysis)
            }
        }
    }

    private fun analyzeChunk(job: AnalysisJob): ChunkAnalysis {
        val runs = ArrayList<SignalRun>()

        if (job.samples.isNotEmpty()) {
            var currentValue = job.samples[0]
            var runStartOffset = 0

            for (index in 1 until job.samples.size) {
                val value = job.samples[index]
                if (value != currentValue) {
                    runs.add(
                        SignalRun(
                            value = currentValue,
                            start = job.start + runStartOffset.toLong(),
                            end = job.start + index.toLong()
                        )
                    )
                    currentValue = value
                    runStartOffset = index
                }
            }

            runs.add(
                SignalRun(
                    value = currentValue,
                    start = job.start + runStartOffset.toLong(),
                    end = job.end
                )
            )
        }

        return ChunkAnalysis(
            start = job.start,
            end = job.end,
            runs = runs
        )
    }

    private fun commitAnalysis(job: AnalysisJob, analysis: ChunkAnalysis) {
        val moreJobs = synchronized(lock) {
            if (job.generation != generation) return
            val record = records[job.id] ?: return
            if (record.revision != job.revision) return
            if (record.status != ChunkStatus.Running) return

            runningJobs.remove(JobKey(job.id, job.revision))

            records[job.id] = record.copy(
                status = ChunkStatus.Committed,
                samples = null,
                analysis = analysis
            )

            redecodeFromLocked(record.start)
            drainSchedulingLocked()
        }

        submitJobs(moreJobs)
    }

    private fun redecodeFromLocked(affectedStart: Long) {
        val restart = checkpoints.floorKey(affectedStart) ?: 0L
        decodeRestartSamples.add(restart)

        checkpoints.tailMap(restart, false).clear()

        var parser = checkpoints[restart]?.copyState() ?: ParserState()
        var expectedStart = restart

        while (true) {
            val chunkId = rangesByStart[expectedStart] ?: break
            val record = records[chunkId] ?: break

            if (record.start != expectedStart) break
            if (record.status != ChunkStatus.Committed) break

            val analysis = record.analysis ?: break

            checkpoints[expectedStart] = parser.copyState()

            for (run in analysis.runs) {
                parser.acceptRun(
                    run = run,
                    samplesPerDit = samplesPerDit,
                    tolerancePercent = tolerancePercent
                )
            }

            expectedStart = record.end
            checkpoints[expectedStart] = parser.copyState()
        }

        contiguousCommittedUntil = expectedStart
        updateDecodedLocked(parser.decoded.toString())
    }

    private fun updateDecodedLocked(newDecoded: String) {
        val oldDecoded = decoded
        if (oldDecoded == newDecoded) return

        if (newDecoded.startsWith(oldDecoded)) {
            val suffix = newDecoded.substring(oldDecoded.length)
            if (suffix.isNotEmpty()) {
                events.add(
                    MorseEvent.Append(
                        sequence = oldDecoded.length,
                        text = suffix
                    )
                )
            }
        } else {
            val prefix = commonPrefixLength(oldDecoded, newDecoded)
            events.add(
                MorseEvent.ReplaceFrom(
                    sequence = prefix,
                    text = newDecoded.substring(prefix)
                )
            )
        }

        decoded = newDecoded
    }

    private fun commonPrefixLength(a: String, b: String): Int {
        val limit = minOf(a.length, b.length)
        var index = 0
        while (index < limit && a[index] == b[index]) {
            index++
        }
        return index
    }

    private class ParserState {
        val decoded: StringBuilder = StringBuilder()
        val pattern: StringBuilder = StringBuilder()
        var invalidCurrentCharacter: Boolean = false
        var pendingRun: SignalRun? = null

        fun copyState(): ParserState {
            val copy = ParserState()
            copy.decoded.append(decoded)
            copy.pattern.append(pattern)
            copy.invalidCurrentCharacter = invalidCurrentCharacter
            copy.pendingRun = pendingRun
            return copy
        }

        fun acceptRun(
            run: SignalRun,
            samplesPerDit: Int,
            tolerancePercent: Int
        ) {
            if (run.length <= 0L) return

            val pending = pendingRun

            if (pending == null) {
                pendingRun = run
                return
            }

            if (pending.value == run.value && pending.end == run.start) {
                pendingRun = SignalRun(
                    value = pending.value,
                    start = pending.start,
                    end = run.end
                )
                return
            }

            finalizeRun(
                run = pending,
                samplesPerDit = samplesPerDit,
                tolerancePercent = tolerancePercent
            )

            pendingRun = run
        }

        private fun finalizeRun(
            run: SignalRun,
            samplesPerDit: Int,
            tolerancePercent: Int
        ) {
            if (run.value) {
                when (classifyTone(run.length, samplesPerDit, tolerancePercent)) {
                    ToneKind.Dit -> pattern.append('.')
                    ToneKind.Dah -> pattern.append('-')
                    null -> invalidCurrentCharacter = true
                }
            } else {
                when (classifyGap(run.length, samplesPerDit, tolerancePercent)) {
                    GapKind.IntraCharacter -> {
                        // Same character continues.
                    }

                    GapKind.Letter -> {
                        finalizeCharacter()
                    }

                    GapKind.Word -> {
                        finalizeCharacter()
                        if (decoded.isNotEmpty() && decoded.last() != ' ') {
                            decoded.append(' ')
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        private fun finalizeCharacter() {
            if (pattern.isEmpty() && !invalidCurrentCharacter) return

            val char =
                if (invalidCurrentCharacter) {
                    '?'
                } else {
                    MORSE_TABLE[pattern.toString()] ?: '?'
                }

            decoded.append(char)
            pattern.clear()
            invalidCurrentCharacter = false
        }
    }

    private data class ChunkRecord(
        val id: String,
        val start: Long,
        val end: Long,
        val revision: Long,
        val status: ChunkStatus,
        val samples: BooleanArray?,
        val analysis: ChunkAnalysis?
    )

    private enum class ChunkStatus {
        Queued,
        Running,
        Committed
    }

    private data class JobKey(
        val id: String,
        val revision: Long
    )

    private data class AnalysisJob(
        val generation: Long,
        val id: String,
        val start: Long,
        val end: Long,
        val revision: Long,
        val samples: BooleanArray
    )

    private data class ChunkAnalysis(
        val start: Long,
        val end: Long,
        val runs: List<SignalRun>
    )

    private data class SignalRun(
        val value: Boolean,
        val start: Long,
        val end: Long
    ) {
        val length: Long
            get() = end - start
    }

    private enum class ToneKind {
        Dit,
        Dah
    }

    private enum class GapKind {
        IntraCharacter,
        Letter,
        Word
    }

    companion object {
        private val MORSE_TABLE: Map<String, Char> = mapOf(
            ".-" to 'A',
            "-..." to 'B',
            "-.-." to 'C',
            "-.." to 'D',
            "." to 'E',
            "..-." to 'F',
            "--." to 'G',
            "...." to 'H',
            ".." to 'I',
            ".---" to 'J',
            "-.-" to 'K',
            ".-.." to 'L',
            "--" to 'M',
            "-." to 'N',
            "---" to 'O',
            ".--." to 'P',
            "--.-" to 'Q',
            ".-." to 'R',
            "..." to 'S',
            "-" to 'T',
            "..-" to 'U',
            "...-" to 'V',
            ".--" to 'W',
            "-..-" to 'X',
            "-.--" to 'Y',
            "--.." to 'Z',
            "-----" to '0',
            ".----" to '1',
            "..---" to '2',
            "...--" to '3',
            "....-" to '4',
            "....." to '5',
            "-...." to '6',
            "--..." to '7',
            "---.." to '8',
            "----." to '9'
        )

        private fun classifyTone(
            length: Long,
            samplesPerDit: Int,
            tolerancePercent: Int
        ): ToneKind? {
            return when {
                isWithinToneRange(length, 1, samplesPerDit, tolerancePercent) -> ToneKind.Dit
                isWithinToneRange(length, 3, samplesPerDit, tolerancePercent) -> ToneKind.Dah
                else -> null
            }
        }

        private fun classifyGap(
            length: Long,
            samplesPerDit: Int,
            tolerancePercent: Int
        ): GapKind {
            val letterLower = lowerBound(3, samplesPerDit, tolerancePercent)
            val wordLower = lowerBound(7, samplesPerDit, tolerancePercent)

            return when {
                length >= wordLower -> GapKind.Word
                length >= letterLower -> GapKind.Letter
                else -> GapKind.IntraCharacter
            }
        }

        private fun isWithinToneRange(
            length: Long,
            units: Int,
            samplesPerDit: Int,
            tolerancePercent: Int
        ): Boolean {
            val lower = lowerBound(units, samplesPerDit, tolerancePercent)
            val upper = upperBound(units, samplesPerDit, tolerancePercent)
            return length in lower..upper
        }

        private fun lowerBound(
            units: Int,
            samplesPerDit: Int,
            tolerancePercent: Int
        ): Long {
            return ceil(
                units.toDouble() *
                    samplesPerDit.toDouble() *
                    (100.0 - tolerancePercent.toDouble()) /
                    100.0
            ).toLong().coerceAtLeast(1L)
        }

        private fun upperBound(
            units: Int,
            samplesPerDit: Int,
            tolerancePercent: Int
        ): Long {
            return floor(
                units.toDouble() *
                    samplesPerDit.toDouble() *
                    (100.0 + tolerancePercent.toDouble()) /
                    100.0
            ).toLong().coerceAtLeast(1L)
        }
    }
}

sealed class MorseEvent {
    data class Append(val sequence: Int, val text: String) : MorseEvent()
    data class ReplaceFrom(val sequence: Int, val text: String) : MorseEvent()
}

data class MorseDebugState(
    val generation: Long,
    val samplesPerDit: Int,
    val tolerancePercent: Int,
    val activeChunks: Set<String>,
    val queuedChunks: Set<String>,
    val runningChunks: Set<String>,
    val committedChunks: Set<String>,
    val decodedText: String,
    val contiguousCommittedUntil: Long,
    val submittedJobCount: Long,
    val retainedSampleCount: Long,
    val decodeRestartSamples: List<Long>
)
